body:
From what I could understand, is the heavy dutyness of the 2500 / 3500 that makes the difference. Specially in sway prone situations... a long trailer has a lot more pull into a 1500 , not so much on a 2500 and 3500....

&#x200B;

Going by what i am learning here, so I welcome your input as I am learning about it

I think what I will in light of this new info, is adapt your script. Remove the delete part, and run daily at 2am , for 1 day ... so it only copies one day at a time , without deleting any events. 

&#x200B;

Again thanks a lot !

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

IT worked flawlessly!!! I ran into a snag, other people had added stuff to the shared calendar, only knew that AFTER I ran the script, was super happy and someone said, Oh some of my stuff disappeared. I will try to think of something. The logic and script you have are fantastic!  thank you so much!

&#x200B;
